\tag{ftip}
\tag{preference}
\tag{data-collection}

\refcardt{Definition}{Preference query selection}{Section 2.2.4}{christiano2017deep}{
\p{Preference learning may choose which trajectory segments or responses to
show to a judge rather than sampling every pair uniformly. The query-selection
procedure assigns candidate comparisons a priority derived from the current
reward-model ensemble and requests labels for selected pairs.}

\p{Because selection depends on the current model and candidate pool, the
resulting comparison data reflect an acquisition policy. Active selection can
concentrate labels on uncertain pairs, but it does not make the collected
comparisons representative of an undeclared target population.}
}
